---
scope: "Delivering a device's scene config OVER ComposeBus itself, so a node with no IP can be configured. Specifies the no-wireless foundation (chunked CONFIG_REQUEST/CONFIG_PUSH sized for classic CAN), the depth-independent leaf contract that makes failure loud, and the selectable config-source strategy that lets a WiFi-capable board bootstrap over HTTP and then kill its radio. Written 2026-08-12 after the firmware transport seam landed and proved UART end-to-end."
audience: "ComposeIO/ComposeUX architects, firmware developers on relay and leaf nodes, and whoever implements the config server on the head node"
boundary: "IN: how config reaches a node that cannot reach bus_storage, the chunk protocol and its sizing constraint, relay behaviour, loop safety, the leaf's failure contract, and config-source selection. OUT: the transport seam itself ([CXC-BOARD-HW-UART-SLAVE], already built), the wire-code table ([BP-TYPE-CODES]), bus_storage's own API, and scene semantics."
not-this: "Not a routing protocol — there are no routing tables, no topology configuration and no hop-count setting. Not a general file-transfer facility; it moves ONE artifact class (a device's scene config) under tight frame budgets. Not a replacement for HTTP config fetch where a board has IP — that path stays and becomes one selectable strategy among several."
